{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
Old Joe [A]Clark, he had a house
Fifteen stories [E]high,
And [A]every story in that house
Was [E]filled with chicken [A]pie.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A]Round and round, old Joe Clark,
[G]Round and round, I say,
[A]Round and round, old Joe Clark,
I [E]haven't long to [A]stay.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
I [A]went down to old Joe's house,
Never been there be[E]fore,
He [A]slept on a feather bed
And [E]I slept on the [A]floor.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: A}
